title: Taking back a reply where the sender sees it asks to fork the sender's note.
pid: 5e1c2774-0186-4c65-bf65-6295fc5b34ba
body: |2-
  Deleting my fork where it stood in place of the message, in my own
  perspective of Top's 'to Jeff', made the server ask to fork 'to Jeff'
  itself. What worked: delete the reply's child, then view the fork as
  its own root and delete it there. Jeff in Emacs would meet the fork
  question. The save's handling is Terry's, overrides Sue's.
